This licence covers the SOURCE CODE, CONFIGURATION AND TEMPLATES in this
repository. It does NOT cover the prose and images under `content/`, which are
licensed separately under CC BY 4.0 — see `content/LICENSE`.

The split is deliberate. MIT over a blog post invites republication of the
author's writing under someone else's name with a one-line notice; CC BY over a
build script is a category error that makes borrowing a config snippet legally
awkward. The repository holds two kinds of thing, and one file cannot describe
both honestly.

